 "capsule": "The state of Jin (晉) was among the most powerful Zhou-era polities, holding the middle Yellow River basin in modern Shanxi and Henan from its traditional 11th-century BCE founding for the Zhou prince Tang Shuyu. Jin dominated Spring and Autumn diplomacy for two centuries, its dukes repeatedly serving as hegemon, until power drained away to the ministerial Han, Zhao, and Wei clans. Their formal partition of Jin's territory in 403 BCE created the Three Jins, marking the conventional start of the Warring States period.",
